ce><Citation>Westermann P. Temperature regulation of methanogenesis in wetlands. Chemosphere, 1993;26(1&#x2013;4): 321&#x2013;328.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Westermann P, Ahring BK. Dynamics of methane production, sulfate reduction and denitrification in a permanently waterlogged alder swamp. Environ Microbiol. 1987;55: 2554&#x2013;2559.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC204145</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">16347472</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Boardman CP, Gauci V, Fox A, Blake S, Beerling DJ. Reduction of the temperature sensitivity of minerotrophic fen methane emissions by simulated glacial atmospheric carbon dioxide starvation. J Geophys Res-Biogeo. 2013;2: 462&#x2013;470.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Updegraff K, Pastor J, Bridgham S D, Johnston CA. Environmental and substrate controls over carbon and nitrogen mineralization in northern wetlands. Ecol Appl. 1995;5(1): 151&#x2013;163</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rath AR, Ramakrishnan B, Sethunathan N. Temperature Dependence of Methane Production in Tropical Rice Soils. Geomicrobiol J. 2002;19: 581&#x2013;592.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>
