0b</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18853791</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ettwig KF, Butler MK, Le Paslier D, Pelletier E, Mangenot S, Kuypers MM, Schreiber F, Dutilh BE, Zedelius J, de Beer D, Gloerich J, Wessels HJ, van Alen T, Luesken F, Wu ML, van de Pas-Schoonen KT, Op den Camp HJ, Janssen-Megens EM, Francoijs KJ, Stunnenberg H, Weissenbach J, Jetten MS, Strous M. 2010. Nitrite-driven anaerobic methane oxidation by oxygenic bacteria. Nature 464:543&#x2013;548. doi: 10.1038/nature08883.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nature08883</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">20336137</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ettwig KF, van Alen T, van de Pas-Schoonen KT, Jetten MS, Strous M. 2009. Enrichment and molecular detection of denitrifying methanotrophic bacteria of the NC10 phylum. Appl Environ Microbiol 75:3656&#x2013;3662. doi: 10.1128/AEM.00067-09.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1128/AEM.00067-09</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2687271</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19329658</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rapp&#xe9; MS, Giovannoni SJ. 2003. The uncultured microbial majority. Annu Rev. Microbiol 57:369&#x2013;394. doi: 10.1146/annurev.micro.57.030502.090759.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1146/annurev.micro.57.030502.090759</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">14527284</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>He Z, Cai C, Shen L, Lou L, Zheng P, Xu X, Hu B. 2015. Effect of inoculum sources on the enrichment of nitrite-dependent anaerobic methane-oxidizing bacteria. Appl Microbiol Biotechnol 99:939&#x2013;946. doi: 10.1007/s00253-014-6033-8.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/s00253-014-6033-8</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">25186148</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hu BL, Shen LD, Lian X, Zhu Q, Liu S, Huang Q, He ZF, Geng S,